 "_about": "scripts/build_make_aliases.py: deterministic matching of a Hebrew manufacturer name (tozar) to the make spellings the open datasets actually contain. Both sides become consonant skeletons: the Hebrew letters through `letters` (already normalized consonants; every option is generated; a geresh ' after a letter selects `geresh`), the Latin make through `latin_rules` (applied in order) with the vowels of `latin_drop` removed and doubled letters collapsed. A source make matches when its skeleton (of the whole name or of its first word) is one the Hebrew name can produce; among several matches the longest skeleton wins, a tie is ambiguous (review list), no match is unmatched (review list). Nothing is guessed: an alias exists only when a source spells it.",
